{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/389404-what-happens-to-the-covers-if-the-demon-dies","id":389404,"title":"What happens to the Covers if the Demon dies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-01T21:30:15-08:00","id":389404,"title":"What happens to the Covers if the Demon dies?","content":"Do they just disappear and become missing persons? does reality revert?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T23:24:16-08:00","id":389474,"title":"","content":"Aside from the cover the demon died in they would go missing for a while then be presumed dead. The cover the demon died in would probably be viewed differently depending on the death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T10:17:17-08:00","id":390034,"title":"","content":"You could set up a subplot around the idea that the covers that were inactive when the demon died are recoverable in some way (even it's a preposterous idea, someone might think it's possible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T11:13:23-08:00","id":390111,"title":"","content":"It's the World of Darkness. Obviously something awful happens. Inactive covers become incomplete persons - retroactively dumped back into reality with all the glitches and gaps any incomplete Cover might have. These entities have some awareness that they aren't all there, and they can kind of upgrade themselves; but they have to do something bad to do it. Maybe eat a demon. Maybe they can't ever become real people, but can steal small bits of the lives of regular humans, gradually improving their Cover by grabbing minor character traits and identity elements like magpies. Maybe they become Dopplegangers. Maybe this only happens to very high level alternate Covers, or all the discarded Covers a Demon loses merge together into some kind of incoherent insane ur-character.<br /> <br /> Maybe they become regular people but with Cover instead of Integrity. Or they're human seeming, but have nothing <i>but</i> Cover, and eventually glitch out of the universe, erased by the cumulative effects of there being nothing else to them but their Cover. Maybe they drop into a bolt-hole like sub space; any demon who knows the right codes can call up dead covers and use them for spare parts, pulling identities off the racks of the dead (stored in what you might call Hell) rather than going for a tailored one. Maybe those empty identities move around a bit in that grey waiting area; maybe they can merge together, struggle to form a composite identity, and them scheme to be released from that Purgatory by an unsuspecting Demon who was just looking for a stock East Asian Male with a history of heart disease and a good credit rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T12:10:35-08:00","id":390192,"title":"","content":"I really liked this idea. So here are my thoughts on making what I called an &quot;Echo&quot;. Other names I thought about were &quot;Hollow People&quot;,&quot;ID Horror&quot; and &quot;Shadow Man&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Echo</b><br /> The Unchained are cosmic entities given flesh, but they exist on many dimensions unseen by mankind. When a Demon then dies it leaves bits of its corpse in these places. Cover, the enigmatic process through which a Demon fakes its human form, is just one piece of the Unchained that gets left behind after death. Most of the time they decay back into the background static of the universe but sometimes they become something far more dangerous: Echoes.<br /> Stories of \u201cshadow men\u201d and \u201cdoppelgangers\u201d populate conspiracy theory websites and ghost stories. They talk about people that aren't all there. They speculate on their being ghosts or demons from another world. Most of the time, they're the bits of people one of the Unchained had hewn together prior to his death.<br /> <br /> The Echo is a cryptid using the following creation recommendations:<br /> A Echo uses the Unchained's Attribute and Skill spread (specifically that of the host demon it came from, but if being used as a solo-monster, then it would be the same as in character creation for Unchained).<br /> Determine the Echo's rank in the same way as any other cryptid.<br /> Adaptations worth considering for your Echo are: Aether Eater, Aether Hive, Occluded.<br /> <br /> <b>Quantum Flesh</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> The Cryptid is made up of the same substances that the God-Machine and Unchained use to form false identities and temporary people. These identities are most often human and usually incomplete, only possessing the details required to have them go unnoticed in the masses of whatever population they're a part of.<br /> <b>System:</b> The Cryptid has a Cover rating like the Unchained and a set character it must pretend to be. This means, like the Unchained, if the cryptid is caught acting out of character it must take a compromise roll. Failure may bring angelic intervention down on the cryptid, mistaking it for a demon, but also important is that when this rating reaches zero the cryptid ceases to exist.<br /> <br /> <b>Identity Eater</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> This is a variation of Aether Eater that works in exactly the same way. The cryptid instead steals Cover from its targets. It may only target living beings of roughly the same archetype. In the case of a human based cryptid, it may steal from a demon's cover, an angel's identity or a human being. Like Aether Eater each successful attack (usually a bite) will steal 1 dot of Cover. This cryptid is especially threatening to the Unchained as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T18:18:39-08:00","id":390786,"title":"","content":"Hmm okay I haven't played Geist so someone else will need to give me the viability of this concept. What about a geist character created from the remains of a cover. (Most likely a soul pact.) I mean the elements of a life are there, the name, the identity, the memories, and probably possession; so is there enough there to have a character in geist who can't make sense of their life because on further inspection they didn't exist till its old occupant died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T21:45:49-08:00","id":391001,"title":"","content":"hmm... I wonder if you could recover the covers if you had the pacts... of course the covers leaving nasty trashed bits is interesting too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T14:41:53-08:00","id":398069,"title":"","content":"I would go with something like the Echoes, except I'd use Stigmatics with Cover instead of Integrity and the Demon's Glitches instead of a &quot;normal&quot; Stigmata.<br /> <br /> I'd keep the &quot;Cover 0 = disappears&quot; thing, because that's awesome.<br /> <br /> But I'd take the opposite tact - they don't know that they're incomplete. Their cover is static from the Demon's death.<br /> <br /> Thing is, people drift over time; you get old, you retire, you divorce, you pick up a hobby. But your cover doesn't. It's still just who you were however many years ago.<br /> <br /> As you live your life, people you knew and loved drift away and stop answering your calls; you could have sworn that you had a cat, but you don't know where she got to. People just gradually <i>forget</i> about you; and sometimes, you forget about you. What was your phone number again? How many brothers and sisters do you have (Was it three? Why can you only remember one of their names?)<br /> <br /> Maybe, if a Demon has pity on you, they'll supply you with a new Cover. But that Cover is never <i>you</i>. Maybe you're alive, yes, but it isn't as <i>you</i>.<br /> <hr /><br /> I guess it all depends on whether or not you want another option for your gribbly monsters, I guess (There isn't a problem with that! It's just that not everything has to have negative consequences in the form of &quot;AND IT EATS PEOPLE!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:38:57-08:00","id":399618,"title":"","content":"I like that Amechra! Furthermore I think they don't even have to be mutually exclusive of one another. One Echo might not realise what it is, and meander through its life much as you describe, while another that discovers what it is or what it could do might become the Echo that eats people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}